Wrote results/ablation_summary.csv (42 rows)

Columns: Δ is the ablated score minus the full-combo reference, so a
POSITIVE Δ means the model scored higher without the category. SE is
the standard error of the AUPRG Δ over the paired folds (ablation fold
k minus reference fold k, the same shared split; sample sd / sqrt(n)).
A |Δ| above 0.005 reads as HARMFUL (Δ > 0) or contributes (Δ < 0)
only when it also exceeds 2 SE, else as within fold noise, and as n/a
with fewer than 2 paired folds; a smaller |Δ| is redundant when `solo`
beats the reference, else no measurable effect. The CSV adds the
paired population sd (delta_auprg_any_paired_sd) and n_paired.
`solo` is that category's winning embedding trained on its own, from the
best-per-category pass — no extra runs needed for it. It is scored
under the row's own variant only where BESTCAT_EXTRA_VARIANTS=1 trained
it (18 rows); otherwise under SELECTION_VARIANT
(pd:pooled), not under the row's kernel / cell-line pooling
(the CSV's solo_variant column says which).
